QA & UAT Evidence Report
Inuka Pulse — Real-Time M&E Dashboard & Web Integration
Beta build, pilot-candidate
1. Scope & Method
This report covers three layers of verification for the Inuka Pulse beta: (a) automated test coverage across the streaming data fabric and dashboard, (b) scripted offline-sync testing for the mobile field-capture layer, and (c) User Acceptance Testing conducted as structured, role-based walkthroughs against the running prototype.
A note on the UAT evidence: for this hackathon submission, UAT was run as an internal dry-run — team members role-played the four field/admin personas below against the live prototype using a fixed test script, rather than live sessions with named Inuka staff. Findings and open items are real and unresolved items are flagged as such. We recommend a short live UAT pass with actual Inuka field officers and M&E/admin staff before pilot rollout, using the same script.
