3. Mobile Offline-Sync Test Log
Executed against the Plus-pillar field capture app, the highest offline-usage pillar. Each scenario was run on a mid-range Android test device with connectivity toggled manually.
Scenario	Steps	Result	Notes
Capture fully offline, reconnect after 15 min	Submit 5 household records offline; restore network	Pass	All 5 synced, identity-matched within 22s of reconnect
Extended offline period (2h)	Submit records offline; hold offline 2h; reconnect	Pass	Queue held locally, synced cleanly on reconnect
Duplicate submission prevention	Submit same record twice offline (accidental double-tap)	Pass	Client-side idempotency key deduped before sync
Conflict: same beneficiary edited on two devices	Edit same record offline on two devices, both reconnect	Pass	Last-write-wins with a flagged diff for officer review
Partial sync interruption	Kill connectivity mid-sync (batch of 12 records)	Pass	Resumed and completed remaining records, no data loss
Low-storage device behavior	Fill device storage to 95% while queue pending	Pass (with note)	Sync succeeded; app did not warn user of low storage — backlog item

28/28 scripted offline-sync scenarios passed functionally; 1 usability backlog item (low-storage warning) logged for Stage 3.
4. User Acceptance Testing Notes
4.1 Persona: Vocational Program Officer
●	Liked that placement outcomes update automatically instead of a monthly manual count against partner employer lists.
●	Requested a filter to view only their own assigned trainee cohort — noted as a a stage enhancement, not a blocker.
4.2 Persona: M&E Manager (cross-pillar)
●	Confirmed the unified beneficiary count matched their manual spot-check for a 20-record sample.
●	Asked for an export-to-Excel button on the Executive View for board-pack preparation — flagged as a quick Stage 3 add, not required for pilot.
4.3 Persona: Plus Field Officer (offline-heavy)
●	Found the offline capture flow familiar coming from the Stage 1 data-collection form.
●	Wants a visible "records waiting to sync" counter on the mobile screen itself, not just on the admin dashboard — logged as a Stage 3 usability item.
4.4 Persona: Communications / Website Admin
●	Confirmed the public widget preview shows no beneficiary-identifying information, satisfying an initial privacy check.
●	Confirmed the embed snippet approach would not require an existing-website rebuild, per their current CMS.
